---
description: Always store user documents via AttachmentStorage (GCS), never base64 in JSON
alwaysApply: true
---

# File / document uploads (GCS attachments)

All user-supplied **files and documents** (enrollment IDs, photos, medical reports, support images, payment proofs, message-letter files, etc.) must go through the **global attachment pipeline**:

- Backend: `AttachmentService.register` → `AttachmentStorage` (`STORAGE_DRIVER=local|gcs`, bucket `GCS_BUCKET`)
- Canonical URL shape: `/api/attachments/:id/download`
- Optional link: `entity_type` + `entity_id` + `purpose` on `attachment_links`

## Do

- Upload with multipart (`file` field) to an attachments endpoint (authenticated `POST /api/attachments`, or a thin public wrapper that still calls `AttachmentService`)
- Persist **attachment id / download path** on the domain row (or link via `attachment_links`)
- Serve downloads only through the attachment controller (auth / signed public where already established)

## Do not

- Embed file bytes as **base64 / data URLs** in JSON request bodies for create/update
- Write new `diskStorage('./uploads/…')` multer routes for product documents when attachments already cover the case
- Mount uploads as public static files
- Invent a second storage stack beside `AttachmentStorage`

## Exceptions (legacy only — do not extend)

- Older `/api/files/…` categories (students/staff photos, subscription-docs, support) until migrated
- When touching those paths, prefer migrating the call site to attachments rather than adding more base64

## New feature checklist

- [ ] Upload uses `AttachmentService` + `AttachmentStorage`
- [ ] Domain payload stores URL/id, not raw bytes
- [ ] `SYSTEM.md` notes the upload path if it is a new public surface
